  "scientific_acceptance": [
    "Three fixed nonlinear Gauss-Newton updates use actual sine-model history and same-stage projected RK4 sensitivities; QR increments and all state/tangent recurrences retain parameter gradients.",
    "The hidden initial state always starts from zero for inference. The true synthetic hidden state appears only in the separate tangent-versus-autograd check.",
    "Independent NumPy truth RHS allocations follow the actual interval-wise ceil rule, including floating clock effects, matching 468912 truth RHS plus 12 energy RHS.",
    "Six frozen cases give one low-energy and one high-initial-speed candidate in each train/val/test role; truth-derived prospective class coverage is a required gate, not an assumed label.",
    "Known and perturbed parameter groups both complete all executable roles regardless of RMSE; no optimizer, parameter fitting, extra noise, old NPZ decode or real-data reading is included.",
    "The existing AND/five-sample loss-of-synchronism rule is reused with the 100 ms origin; unsettled and numerical failures remain explicit, overall accuracy is withheld when unresolved, and balanced accuracy requires both true classes.",
    "Complete gradient, known-parameter recovery, trajectory refinement and stability correctness are distinct checks; perturbed prediction accuracy is descriptive."
